    <!-- ================= HALAMAN TOKYO ================= -->
    <div class="page" id="tokyo">
        <header>
            <h1>Tokyo, Japan 🇯🇵</h1>
            <p>Tokyo was the city where our group first realized that getting lost on purpose can be the best part of a trip. Every alley hid a ramen shop, a vending machine, or a shrine we had never heard of.</p>
        </header>

        <main>
            <section id="landmarks">
                <h2>Landmarks 🗼</h2>
                <figure>
                    <img src="shibuya.jpg" alt="Shibuya Crossing at night">
                    <figcaption>Shibuya Crossing at night, when the whole street seems to move at once.</figcaption>
                </figure>
                <p>We spent one evening at Senso-ji in Asakusa, then took the train to Shinjuku to watch the city lights from the observation deck.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="culinary">
                <h2>Culinary Delights 🍜</h2>
                <p>Our favorite discovery was a tiny ramen counter with only eight seats. The chef nodded at us and served a bowl that none of us will ever forget.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="culture">
                <h2>Cultural Experiences 🎌</h2>
                <p>We joined a tea ceremony in Kyoto, a short trip from Tokyo, and learned how every movement carries meaning.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="virtual-tour">
                <h2>Virtual Tour 🎥</h2>
                <iframe width="560" height="315"
                    src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/VIDEO_ID"
                    title="Walking tour of Tokyo"
                    allowfullscreen>
                </iframe>
            </section>

            <section id="reflections">
                <h2>Personal Reflections 💭</h2>
                <p>Tokyo taught us that a city can be busy and calm at the same time. It is the place we still talk about first when we meet.</p>
            </section>
        </main>
    </div>

    <!-- ================= HALAMAN PARIS ================= -->
    <div class="page" id="paris">
        <header>
            <h1>Paris, France 🇫🇷</h1>
            <p>Paris was the city where our group learned to slow down. We stopped rushing between landmarks and started spending whole afternoons in cafés, watching the city go by.</p>
        </header>

        <main>
            <section id="landmarks-paris">
                <h2>Landmarks 🗼</h2>
                <figure>
                    <img src="eiffel.webp" alt="Eiffel Tower seen from the Seine river">
                    <figcaption>The Eiffel Tower glowing over the Seine, seen from our evening walk.</figcaption>
                </figure>
                <p>We climbed up to Montmartre to see Sacré-Cœur at sunset, then walked back down through the narrow streets toward the river.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="culinary-paris">
                <h2>Culinary Delights 🥐</h2>
                <p>Every morning started with a fresh croissant and a small cup of strong coffee at a corner bakery. In the evening we shared a plate of cheese and bread by the Seine, which became our favorite ritual.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="culture-paris">
                <h2>Cultural Experiences 🎨</h2>
                <p>We spent a rainy afternoon at the Louvre and another at a small gallery in Le Marais. Both made us appreciate how art lives in everyday street corners as much as in museums.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="virtual-tour-paris">
                <h2>Virtual Tour 🎥</h2>
                <iframe width="560" height="315"
                    src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/VIDEO_ID"
                    title="Walking tour of Paris"
                    allowfullscreen>
                </iframe>
            </section>

            <section id="reflections-paris">
                <h2>Personal Reflections 💭</h2>
                <p>Paris reminded us that a trip does not have to be packed with plans to be unforgettable. Some of our best memories came from doing nothing at all, together.</p>
            </section>
        </main>
    </div>

    <!-- ================= HALAMAN YOGYAKARTA ================= -->
    <div class="page" id="yogyakarta">
        <header>
            <h1>Yogyakarta, Indonesia 🇮🇩</h1>
            <p>Yogyakarta was the city that felt most like home. Its warm people, its art, and its slow mornings made us feel welcome from the moment we arrived.</p>
        </header>

        <main>
            <section id="landmarks-yogya">
                <h2>Landmarks 🛕</h2>
                <figure>
                    <img src="borobudur.jpeg" alt="Borobudur temple at sunrise">
                    <figcaption>Borobudur at sunrise, when the stone temple slowly turns golden.</figcaption>
                </figure>
                <p>We also visited the Keraton, the royal palace in the city center, and walked through Taman Sari, the old water castle with its hidden pools and passageways.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="culinary-yogya">
                <h2>Culinary Delights 🍛</h2>
                <p>Our favorite meal was gudeg, sweet jackfruit cooked slowly with coconut milk and eaten with rice and egg. We also loved sate klatak and a warm cup of wedang uwuh in the evening.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="culture-yogya">
                <h2>Cultural Experiences 🎭</h2>
                <p>We watched a wayang kulit shadow puppet performance late into the night and tried batik painting in a small studio. Each experience showed us how much patience and story live in Javanese art.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="virtual-tour-yogya">
                <h2>Virtual Tour 🎥</h2>
                <iframe width="560" height="315"
                    src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/VIDEO_ID"
                    title="Walking tour of Yogyakarta"
                    allowfullscreen>
                </iframe>
            </section>

            <section id="reflections-yogya">
                <h2>Personal Reflections 💭</h2>
                <p>Yogyakarta taught us that hospitality can be the most memorable part of a trip. Long after the temples faded from view, we remembered the friendly faces who made us feel at home.</p>
            </section>
        </main>
    </div>

    <!-- ================= HALAMAN GALLERY ================= -->
